Skip the entity-removal event when nothing is listening.

CraftEventFactory#callEntityRemoveEvent sits in Entity#setRemoved - the single path every entity
takes on its way out of the world. Mob deaths, item and XP orb despawns, projectiles expiring,
entities dropped when a chunk unloads: all of it lands here.

The method returns void, and getBukkitEntity() creates the CraftEntity wrapper when one does not
exist yet, so with no listener registered this was allocating wrappers for entities that were
already leaving. This project's own tuned config makes it hotter still - monsters despawn at 28/48,
items and arrows at 15 seconds - so the removal rate is deliberately high.

The listener check goes first, ahead of the existing player/null-cause/generation guards, so the
common case exits immediately.

--- a/paper-server/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/event/CraftEventFactory.java
+++ b/paper-server/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/event/CraftEventFactory.java
@@ -2259,6 +2259,10 @@
     public static void callEntityRemoveEvent(Entity entity, EntityRemoveEvent.Cause cause) {
+        if (EntityRemoveEvent.getHandlerList().getRegisteredListeners().length == 0) {
+            return;
+        }
         if (entity instanceof ServerPlayer) {
             return; // Don't call for player
         }
